{#-
  Purpose: OPTIONAL follow-up probe. We already know IdKey works via RockEntity
  entity lookups ({% schedule id:'3912' %}{{ schedule.IdKey }}{% endschedule %}).
  This checks whether a Lava FILTER can convert a raw integer id straight to an
  IdKey, which would remove the need for per-card entity lookups entirely.

  Known-good values to match against:
    Group    345104 -> bg31BgMbYo
    Location 36682  -> Vm3W4JoY7r
    Schedule 3912   -> z0YnJDwYXo

  HOW TO RUN: paste into an HTML Content block with RockEntity in
  "Enabled Lava Commands". Unknown filters render blank rather than erroring,
  so this is safe. Delete the block afterwards.

  WHAT TO REPORT: the rendered output. Any line showing a 10-character hash
  is a win; all-blank means no such filter and we use entity lookups.
-#}

<h3>Part A — candidate filter names (Schedule 3912, want z0YnJDwYXo)</h3>
<pre>
IdToKey (typed):   [{{ 3912 | IdToKey:'Rock.Model.Schedule' }}]
IdToKey (bare):    [{{ 3912 | IdToKey }}]
ToIdKey (typed):   [{{ 3912 | ToIdKey:'Rock.Model.Schedule' }}]
ToIdKey (bare):    [{{ 3912 | ToIdKey }}]
IdKey:             [{{ 3912 | IdKey }}]
HashId:            [{{ 3912 | HashId }}]
EntityIdToKey:     [{{ 3912 | EntityIdToKey:'Rock.Model.Schedule' }}]
</pre>

<h3>Part B — is the hash global, or per entity type?</h3>
{#- If the same integer yields the SAME hash across different entity types,
    the hasher is id-only. That means one lookup table works for everything,
    and it also tells us a typed filter argument is unnecessary. -#}
<pre>
Group    14: [{% group    id:'14' %}{{ group.IdKey }}{% endgroup %}]
Location 14: [{% location id:'14' %}{{ location.IdKey }}{% endlocation %}]
Schedule 14: [{% schedule id:'14' %}{{ schedule.IdKey }}{% endschedule %}]
Campus   14: [{% campus   id:'14' %}{{ campus.IdKey }}{% endcampus %}]
</pre>
<p><em>All identical => hasher is global/id-only. Different => hash is salted per
entity type, and any lookup must be done against the correct type.</em></p>
